GDPR ARTICLE 17 – RIGHT TO ERASURE (‘RIGHT TO BE FORGOTTEN’) [...] 1. The data subject shall have the right to obtain from the controller the erasure of personal data concerning them without undue delay where one of the following grounds applies:
   (a) the personal data are no longer necessary;
   (b) the data subject withdraws consent;
   (c) the data subject objects to processing and there are no overriding legitimate grounds;
   (d) the personal data have been unlawfully processed;
